    "description": "Bayonne Energy Center is a gas-fired generating facility located in Bayonne, New Jersey. Its customer market is New York City, where the plant sells electricity, capacity, and ancillary services through a dedicated subsea cable connection into NYISO Zone J. The business follows an asset-heavy generation model with wholesale market exposure rather than a regulated utility model. Morgan Stanley describes the facility as a 660 MW dual-fuel plant and states that it acquired the asset in 2018 and has managed it through its TigerGenCo power asset management platform. The plant serves a tightly constrained urban load pocket and is positioned as dispatchable support for New York City's grid reliability. In March 2026, Morgan Stanley Infrastructure Partners announced an agreement to sell the asset, but reviewed sources indicate that closing had not yet been completed.",
